            explore sample data and simulated payments.
          </p>
          <p>
            A connected till needs the shop's configured backend, a pairing code
            from its administrator and cashier access. Card payments also need a
            supported, configured terminal and a payment-provider agreement. Ask
            your shop administrator for access. The
            <a href="/docs/pos/fyrstu-skref/">iPad setup guide</a> is in
            Icelandic.
          </p>
          <h2>If a connection or payment stops</h2>
          <p>
            Do not retry a charge or clear the device's data while its outcome
            is unknown. Keep the transaction reference and ask your manager to
            verify the final result with the payment provider. A connection
            error or app termination does not prove that payment failed. Ask
            your administrator to replace an expired pairing code; never send
            the code in a support request.
          </p>
          <h2>Purchases, refunds and payment terminals</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about a purchase or refund, contact the shop where you
            made the purchase. For a payment-terminal issue, follow your
            merchant support arrangement with Teya or the relevant payment
            provider.
          </p>
          <h2>Free app</h2>
          <p>
            The app is free to download. Payment processing and connected
            third-party services may require separate agreements and fees.
          </p>
          <h2 id="data-requests">Privacy and data deletion</h2>
          <p>
            Send requests about personal information, retention or data deletion
            to <a href="mailto:depill@depill.is">depill@depill.is</a>. See the{" "}
            <a href="/pos/privacy/en/">Supergut POS privacy notice</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Include the shop, your relationship to it and whether you are
            requesting access, correction or deletion. We verify identity and
            authority before disclosing or changing records. Do not send ID
            documents or sensitive data in your initial request. An
            administrator can revoke device or staff access; this does not
            automatically erase retained transaction or accounting records.
          </p>
